                        "glosses": [
                            "Unworthy of merit; not deserving of merit; not meritorious."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f4dae3cd-bc8e-44c6-a138-995766da5e05",
                                "sense_id": "5f4b390a-947b-3875-90ba-b0f1d497cc0d",
                                "text": "Their acceptance indeed, as a formula, may show a willing and tractable spirit, and they may to that extent have a value : but such acceptance differs of course from belief in being admittedly a voluntary act, and not a mere immeritorious and reluctant yielding to the brute weight of evidence."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "45b85f90-49d5-447d-b03d-6d5adca71a07",
                                "sense_id": "5f4b390a-947b-3875-90ba-b0f1d497cc0d",
                                "text": "As long as the defence is credible and can be reasonably substantiated so that the counterclaim is not evidently immeritorious, the attacked party has little to lose, and may gain time."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
